effe, 1988 (1988.130.1).","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Not recorded Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks. Claudia O'Keeffe was one of the artist's four sisters. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"11 3/4 x 9 3/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"Claudia O'Keeffe, Beverly Hills, California, gift, after 1968; Estate of Claudia O'Keeffe, 1984 \n(Source: Lynes, 1999)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"New Mexico Museum of Art","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Claudia O'Keeffe was one of the artist's four sisters. A young girl with brown eyes and short brown hair looks out at the viewer at the center of this oval-shaped composition. The girl wears a white shirt or dress with a square neckline.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Untitled (Claudia O'Keeffe), 1907–1908","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"h